I1
sV1.1 We may obtain non-personally identifiable information from you. Non-personally identifiable information is information that usually cannot by itself be used to identify a particular person or entity, and may include: the Internet Protocol (IP) address, unique device identifiers, operating system, mobile network information, browser type, browsing and/or downloading activity and non-precise device location information.
p21
I1
sVWe don\u2019t sell your personally identifiable information to third parties.
